SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The cchhoowwnn utility is compliant with the  specification.

     The ability to specify _g_r_o_u_p without _o_w_n_e_r is an extension to that speci‐
     fication.

     Some non-BSD systems may allow the (non-privileged) owner of a file to
     change its ownership.

     Previous versions of the cchhoowwnn utility used the dot (‘.’) character to
     distinguish the group name.  This was changed when the utility was first
     standardised in IEEE Std 1003.2-1992 (“POSIX.2”) to be a colon (‘:’)
     character to allow user and group names to contain the dot character,
     though the dot separator still remains supported due to widely required
     backwards compatibility.

